# 0037 XeMTL plugin: numbered surface marks, late-release log
#
# Base:  plugin/ after 0005 + 0006 + 0007 + 0026 + 0031 (XeGfx 0.0.35 · 497d521e)
# Files: plugin/{NVMTLEventSync.m, nvmtl_vk.c, nvmtl_vk.h}
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0037-plugin-numbered-marks.patch
# Build: XeMTLDriver a054790c7708 (ddca6dfe9d76 after ad-hoc signing; needs accel 0036 for selector 13)
#
# Numbered marks: each WindowServer command buffer marks the surfaces it writes through selector 13 at commit and keeps
# each surface's mark number; when it has finished with a surface it releases its own number at once, instead of the
# kernel's one bit waiting for every overlapping command buffer.  The publication ordering of the earlier counted holds
# is unchanged.  An accelerator without selector 13 keeps the old protocol (selector 1/2, one mark per surface).
#
# Late-release log: a composite whose mark is released 30 ms or more after commit logs one line with commit ->
# scheduled -> GPU done -> release, its part count and event waits (first 200, then every 32nd).  This is what showed
# the overlapping command buffers: late releases were all "scheduled +0, one part, no waits".
